  "text": " Everyone's making AI animated reels with Claudecode right now, but nobody's showing you how. So I'll show you everything, every step you need to make reels like this one. First, you need Claudecode. Don't use it in the browser. Download the desktop app. Next, make a folder on your computer and call it AI Video Editor. That's where your skill files and every finished reel will live. Then start a new Claudecode chat, choose local and select that folder. Now Claude can read and write your files. Claude needs a few tools to animate, voice and render, so tell it to check your setup. It installs what's missing and walks you through every click. Now the fun part. Type what the reel is about in one line. Something like, make a reel about why airplane food tastes so bland. It writes the script, records the voiceover, animates every scene, times the captions to every word and checks its own motion before you see it. If something feels off, just tell it, like you would a reel editor, and it fixes it. That's the entire workflow. And if you want my personal system, the 221 files behind every reel on this account, comment SKILL and I'll send it to you.",
